Mode builds on the following open source work. Each is used under its own license;
see the linked project for the full terms.

Code adapted into Mode
- OAuthLanguageModels by finnvoor (CC0 1.0): the Claude sign-in and Messages protocol
  adapted in engine/llm (https://github.com/finnvoor/OAuthLanguageModels).

Libraries
- isideload (MIT OR Apache-2.0): signing and installing Mode from Mode Setup
  (https://github.com/nab138/isideload).
- idevice (MIT): talking to the iPhone over USB and CoreDevice
  (https://github.com/jkcoxson/idevice).
- Tauri (MIT OR Apache-2.0): the Mode Setup app (https://tauri.app).
- Kotlin, kotlinx.coroutines, kotlinx.serialization, kotlinx-datetime (Apache-2.0),
  JetBrains (https://github.com/Kotlin).
- Ktor (Apache-2.0): networking (https://ktor.io).
- SQLDelight (Apache-2.0): the on-phone database (https://github.com/cashapp/sqldelight).
- SKIE (Apache-2.0): Swift interop for Kotlin (https://skie.touchlab.co).
- The Rust crates listed in desktop/Cargo.lock and native/*/Cargo.lock, each under its
  own license.

Fonts
- Bricolage Grotesque (SIL Open Font License 1.1), bundled in the design system
  (https://github.com/ateliertriay/bricolage).

Apps Mode works with (not bundled; installed separately by the user)
- SideStore (https://sidestore.io): optional, renews Mode on a free Apple account.
- LocalDevVPN: used by the free build to reach the iPhone's CoreDevice services.
